From 63bbd2bc0f256870909d42a1a580c17dc51299a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bherbruck <brennen.herbruck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:57:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Fit to Models' cylinder is snug - the part's radius plus
 the allowance

The cylinder fit took its diameter from the padded footprint's diagonal,
so a round part of radius R got a ~1.41 R bar, and since #130 every
auto-fitted lathe setup roughs passes in air. It now takes the models'
largest horizontal distance from the fit's axis (a turned part's revolved
max radius) plus the margin: still containing every vertex, never larger
than before.

Fixes #230

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
